# GREYSCALE -- sixteen even steps, black to white.
# A ramp, not a theme: entry n is n/15 of full white, so anything
# drawn by index gets a shade rather than a hue.  The COLOR line
# below picks near-white on black, because on a ramp the shell's usual
# 7 on 6 is two neighbouring greys and cannot be read.
#
# One exception: entry 1 is the shell's highlight (DIR's header and
# directories, labels, the banner) -- white on the VIC-II -- so it is
# white here too, or those print black on black.  Text is E, one step
# down, so the highlight still stands out.
#
# index rr gg bb, all hex.  A file only changes the entries it names.
#
COLOR E 0
0 00 00 00
1 FF FF FF
2 22 22 22
3 33 33 33
4 44 44 44
5 55 55 55
6 66 66 66
7 77 77 77
8 88 88 88
9 99 99 99
A AA AA AA
B BB BB BB
C CC CC CC
D DD DD DD
E EE EE EE
F FF FF FF
